\subsection{Mixture of Experts with Multi-head Attention}

We propose a novel multi-task learning framework called Mixture of Experts with Multi-head Attention (MEMA) see Figure~\ref{fig:figure09}, which aims to precisely capture the differences between tasks. Compared to the classic MMoE method~\cite{MMoE},
the key advantage lies in the multi-head self-attention mechanism, which guarantees that the disentangled representations derive from the same hidden space, 
thereby enabling more accurate soft decomposition results.
More specifically, the output of task $k$ can be represented as follows:
\begin{equation}
f^{k}(x) = \mathrm{FFN}(\mathrm{Concat}(\mathrm{head_1},\cdots,\mathrm{head_n}))^k
\end{equation}
where $\mathrm{head}$ represents scaled dot-product attention, $\mathrm{Concat}$ means concatenation, $\mathrm{FFN}$ refers to feed-forward network,.

