For a linear maximal length CA over GF($q$), the length of the cycle is $q^n-1$. Theorem~\ref{theorem:mlcagf(q)} relates the maximal length CA and primitive polynomial over GF($q$). The characteristic polynomial of the CA of Figure~\ref{figure:transition2} is $x^3+x^2+2x+1\pmod3$, which is primitive over GF(3).  

