\noindent This equation system is inconsistent, since its Chebyshev distance, see (\ref{eq:Nabla}), is equal to 0.04. As we have $0.04 < \tau_1$, the training data sample is assessed as reliable with respect to $\tau_1$ (Definition \ref{def:reliabletau}). We construct a consistent equation system using Definition \ref{def:reduced-es}:
\begin{equation}\label{ex15:cons-eq-sys-1}
