\label{sec:appendix:posslearn:withDSL}

To complete our empirical study, we also analyzed the characteristics and performance of the possibilistic learning method (Method \ref{meth:learningincascade}) applied to the MNIST Addition-$k$ problems with $k \in \{1,2,4,15,100\}$ when $\Pi$-NeSy takes advantage of  DeepSoftLog's CNN, yielding to the results presented in Table \ref{tab:deepsoftlog_cnn_mnist_add_results}. We reuse the notations given in Section \ref{sec:appendix:expadd}.

For MNIST Addition-$k$ problems with $k \in \{1, 2, 4, 15, 100\}$, both $\Pi$-NeSy-1 and $\Pi$-NeSy-2 consistently utilize the same threshold value of $4.12\times10^{-8}$ for Thresholds \#1, \#2, and \#3, as in the normal settings (see Subsection \ref{subsec:appendix:posslearn:mnistadd}). This threshold value is the smallest in the set $\mathcal{T}$ of candidate thresholds, see (\ref{eq:setTvalidationstep}).




