We focus on graph parameters, including maximum matching, degeneracy, diameter, chromatic number, vertex-cover,  maximum independent set, and maximum clique. 
For each of these parameters, we aim at certifying whether it is at most, or at least a given threshold value~$k$ (which may be fixed, or given as input). For instance, $\MM_{\leq k}$ (resp., $\MM_{\geq k}$) is the boolean predicate corresponding to whether the input graph given as a stream has a maximum matching of size at most~$k$ (resp., at least~$k$). 

