The previous example may be easily generalized as follows.

\begin{theorem}\label{genexfrob}
Let $M\in {\rm M}_n(\KK)$, and let $\KK^n=V_1\oplus\cdots\oplus V_t$ be a decomposition of $\KK^n$ into cyclic subspaces such that the restriction of $\rho_M$ to $V_i$ has minimal polynomial $\Theta_i$.   

  Let $P\in\LL[x]$, and let $\Cc=\ker(P(M))$. Let $\Lambda=\{ i\in\left\llbracket 1,t\right\rrbracket \mid {\rm gcd}(P, \Theta_i)\neq 1\}$.


  Assume that ${\rm gcd}(P,\Theta_i)$ has degree $1$ for all $i\in\Lambda$, and let ${\bf w}_i\in\LL^{d_i}$ be the vector of coefficients of $\displaystyle\frac{\Theta_i}{{\rm gcd}(P,\Theta_i)}$, where $d_i\defegal\deg(\Theta_i)$.

  Then, $\Cc$ has dimension $\vert \Lambda\vert$, and  for all $r\in\left\llbracket 1, \vert\Lambda\vert\right\rrbracket$, we have $$M_r(\Cc)=\underset{\substack{J\subset\left\llbracket 1,\vert\Lambda\vert\right\rrbracket \\ \vert J\vert =r}}{\min} \left(\sum_{j\in J}{\rm wt}_R({\bf w}_j)\right).$$
\end{theorem}

