Figure~\ref{fig:performance_vs_power} illustrates the general proportionality between operations per second and accelerator power consumption, with some exceptions. This correlation is logical because increased operations per second typically leads to higher resource utilization on an FPGA, resulting in increased power consumption. However, it should be noted that reported power consumptions were often estimated rather than measured, focusing primarily on on-chip or accelerator power. Given its significance for space applications, we advocate reporting measured power consumption. From this metric, we can determine the operations per second per watt, which is particularly valuable for onboard spacecraft implementations as it delineates the relationship between accelerator performance and power efficiency.
