Following the setwise setup in~\citet{DBLP:conf/sigir/ZhuangZKZ24}, we utilize the Flan-T5 \cite{DBLP:journals/jmlr/ChungHLZTFL00BW24} as the backbone for most of the LLM-based rerankers except for IRL and Tourrank as these two methods require a longer context than Flan-T5’s input limitation allows. For IRL and Tourrank, we employ the Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct model. To compare our estimated FLOPs with those reported by open-source packages, we also include Qwen2.5~\cite{yang2025qwen3} (3B, 7B, 14B), which implements group query attention instead of multi-head attention. For all LLM-based rerankers, we report their performance using the new metrics on the TREC-DL19 and DL20 datasets~\cite{craswell2020overview}. The top 100 documents are retrieved using Pyserini’s BM25~\cite{lin2021pyserini}.


For FLOPs measurement, we utilize DeepSpeed’s FLOPs profiler~\cite{DBLP:conf/kdd/RasleyRRH20} and calflops~\cite{calflops} profilers and find identical results from both sources.

