\section{Conclusion and Future Works}

Due to limitation of existing metrics in evaluating the efficiency-effectiveness tradeoff of large language models as rerankers, we propose two metrics RPP and QPP to quantify the model performance. In addition, we provide a calculator through a closed-form and interpretable formula to compute the FLOPs and validate this estimation through experiments on existing decoder-only and encoder-decoder model architectures. The estimated FLOP count exhibits a strong linear correlation with the actual measured values, allowing it to approximate real-world computational cost even without model execution. Future work includes conducting a linear regression between the real and estimated FLOP counts to refine our estimation and adapting to more advanced architectures. 

